@format 1
@id relay.execute-durable-plan
@title Execute durable Auto-relay plan
@area 6. Relay and routing
@entry submit
@summary Snapshot a complete Auto-relay graph at submission and materialize later stages without consulting mutable tabs.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@allow-cycle true
@related queue.add-work, relay.deliver-output, project.restore-session
@tag relay
@tag persistence
@tag plan

@alias courier = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.LCourier
@alias plan = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.LRelayPlan
@alias planstore = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.LRelayPlanStore

[submit] User submits work with a relay target <input>
- Group immediate work by cohort and check for an existing saved plan before inspecting the live route @ courier.LCourierScheduleAdd(...)
> route

[route] Select routing authority <decision>
- Load any durable plan already owned by the cohort @ planstore.LRelayPlanRead(...)
? "Saved plan exists" > normalize
? "New live target" > capture
? "No target or Finish target" > direct

[normalize] Normalize saved-plan work <process>
- Resolve original-tab or stable-stage source and target identities against the saved stages @ courier.LCourierScheduleAdd(...)
- Prefer the saved source stage's next stage when assigning the stable target @ courier.LCourierScheduleAdd(...)
> wait

[direct] Keep direct route <output>
- Preserve the empty or Finish target without creating a durable stage graph @ courier.LCourierScheduleAdd(...)
= Work is scheduled without a new saved plan.

[capture] Capture reachable stages <process>
- Give every stage a new stable ID and clone its layout, processing, export, automatic, Merge, and Funnel state @ plan.LRelayPlanCreate(...)
- Translate ordinary edges and Funnel targets from temporary tab identities to stable stage identities @ plan.LRelayPlanCreate(...)
> persist

[persist] Save before scheduling <decision>
- Atomically save the plan in the active workspace @ planstore.LRelayPlanSave(...)
? "Plan saved" > assign
? "Plan cannot be saved" > legacy

[assign] Assign stable entry <process>
- Put the plan's entry-stage ID on immediate work before adding it to the schedule @ courier.LCourierScheduleAdd(...)
> wait

[wait] Predecessor executes <process>
- Keep future stages as snapshots until completed predecessor work becomes eligible for dispatch @ courier.LCourierDispatch(...)
> arrive

[arrive] Resolve saved stage <decision>
- Load the cohort plan by batch ID @ planstore.LRelayPlanRead(...)
- Resolve the work's stable target stage from that plan @ courier.LCourierOutputAdd(...)
? "Automatic ordinary stage" > materialize
? "Merge stage still has reachable work" > collect
? "Merge stage is ready" > materialize
? "Funnel stage" > branch
? "Automatic was disabled at submission" > checkpoint

[materialize] Materialize from snapshot <process>
- Construct a detached workspace from the saved layout and export preset @ courier.LCourierPlanStageArrive(...)
- Require the detached surface to expose both an action and a list before it can schedule work @ courier.LCourierPlanStageArrive(...)
> materialize-ready

[materialize-ready] Can the saved stage run? <decision>
? "Action and list are available" > queue-stage
? "Detached surface cannot run work" > consumed

[queue-stage] Queue materialized work <process>
- Apply the stable source-stage and next-stage identities to the detached action @ courier.LCourierPlanStageArrive(...)
- Add distinct pending inputs and run all Merge inputs or the selected ordinary inputs @ courier.LCourierPlanStageArrive(...)
- Clear persisted inputs after invoking the stage action @ courier.LCourierPlanStageArrive(...)
> wait [loop]

[collect] Persist Merge inputs <storage>
- Retain cohort inputs until no pending or undelivered work can still reach the Merge stage @ courier.LCourierPlanMergeBlocked(...)
> wait [loop]

[branch] Apply saved Funnel rules <process>
- Match the filename against the snapshotted rules @ plan.LRelayFunnelTargetRead(...)
- Continue recursively at the resolved saved target stage @ courier.LCourierPlanStageArrive(...)
> funnel-result

[funnel-result] Did a saved rule resolve? <decision>
? "Target stage exists" > arrive [loop]
? "No target stage exists" > consumed

[checkpoint] Pause plan-owned input <storage>
- Persist the input at the stage and optionally mirror it into the original tab when that view still exists @ courier.LCourierPlanStageArrive(...)
> paused

[paused] Plan paused <output>
= The stage input remains durable, and later checkbox or tab changes do not implicitly resume or redirect the submitted plan.

[consumed] Stage continuation stops <output>
= The input is cleared from a Funnel stage with no saved target, or remains recorded when a detached stage cannot expose runnable controls; no downstream work is queued on this pass.

[legacy] Compatible fallback <error>
- Retain live-tab routing when the durable plan cannot be constituted or persisted @ courier.LCourierScheduleAdd(...)
= Work remains schedulable; persistence failures are logged by the plan store, while an unavailable live route may fall back silently.
